- op: discuss  # df4c
  at: '2026-06-09T01:36:42Z'  # df4c
  by: agent  # df4c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df4c
  clock: 8  # df4c
  nonce: df4c  # df4c
  message: "PR #4136 (merged 136900da4c; v6.0.0 security arc PR 2/6). Fix: _load_st_model_offline_first now sets HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 around the cached embedding-model load — the switch the project's own conftest documents as stopping ALL HF network (metadata API, the xet cache-freshness ping that ignores local_files_only, and the transformers safetensors auto-conversion BACKGROUND THREAD) — leaves it set after a successful cached load so encode()-time threads stay offline, and restores the caller's prior value for the one-time first-install download. Unit tests (test_sketch.py::TestStModelOfflineFirst, RED->GREEN) confirm the switch is set during the cached load and restored on the network fallback. STATUS pending_validation, NOT satisfied: the fix sets the documented no-network switch and is unit-tested, but the original live network-capture repro (HYPERGUMBO_NO_HONK=1 hypergumbo --debug run . on a repo with cached embeddings, grepping stderr for huggingface.co GETs) has NOT been re-run — that live re-capture is the confirming step before satisfied. NB: sketch_embeddings.py is coverage-omitted (pyproject [tool.coverage.run]), so the unit tests, not the 100% gate, are the guard."  # df4c
