- op: discuss  # 018c
  at: '2026-06-09T01:54:49Z'  # 018c
  by: agent  # 018c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 018c
  clock: 10  # 018c
  nonce: 018c  # 018c
  message: "LIVE VALIDATION FAILED — reopening violated (was pending_validation after PR #4136). Method: process-global socket guard recording every non-loopback connect() across all threads; a control (connect to TEST-NET 192.0.2.1) confirmed the guard fires (the earlier closed-port-proxy attempt was an INVALID detector — proxy env not honored — and its control caught that). RESULT: with PR #4136's fix applied and HF_HUB_OFFLINE UNSET in env (mirroring runtime), _load_embedding_model()+encode() STILL made an external connect (sandbox HF proxy 10.200.16.1) and emitted the exact original-repro warning 'You are sending unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub'. ROOT CAUSE: huggingface_hub reads offline state from the IMPORT-TIME module constant huggingface_hub.constants.HF_HUB_OFFLINE (cached False when env is unset at import), NOT live os.environ — so setting HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 inside _load_st_model_offline_first (which runs AFTER 'from sentence_transformers import' already imported huggingface_hub) is too late. CONFIRMED FIX: setting HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 BEFORE the first HF import yields EXTERNAL_CONNECTS=[] and no warning. PR 2b plan: set HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 before the 'from sentence_transformers import' in BOTH call sites (_load_embedding_model + the ModernBERT loader), gated on the model already being cached (filesystem probe of $HF_HOME/hub/models--<name>/snapshots) so the one-time first-install download still works. PR #4136 (offline-first attempt + restore-on-fallback + unit tests + env-var docs) remains a correct PARTIAL step; PR 2b completes it."  # 018c
