- op: discuss  # b984
  at: '2026-06-09T02:47:51Z'  # b984
  by: agent  # b984
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b984
  clock: 12  # b984
  nonce: b984  # b984
  message: "SATISFIED with positive live evidence. Completing fix merged in PR #4139 (5d6e46b955; v6.0.0 security arc PR 2b), after PR #4136 (partial). Fix: HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 is now set BEFORE the first huggingface_hub import at all three import sites (_has_sentence_transformers / _load_embedding_model / _load_modernbert_model) via _ensure_hf_offline_for_cached_models(), gated on every embedding model already being cached (_hf_model_is_cached fs probe) so the one-time first-install download is preserved. POSITIVE EVIDENCE (live network capture, process-global socket guard recording non-loopback connect()s across all threads; control verified the guard fires on TEST-NET 192.0.2.1): on the PATCHED code with HF_HUB_OFFLINE UNSET in env and both models cached, _load_embedding_model()+encode() produced EXTERNAL_CONNECTS=[] and ZERO 'unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub' warnings — vs the pre-2b capture which connected to the HF proxy (10.200.16.1) and emitted the warning. Root cause was import-timing: huggingface_hub freezes constants.HF_HUB_OFFLINE at import, ignoring later os.environ. Regression guards: subprocess import-timing tests (test_sketch.py::TestHfOfflineBeforeImport) assert the constant flips True/False by cache state; gated on huggingface_hub availability (absent in base CI). Residual (documented in spec): the transient partial-cache window still permits HF metadata traffic, since the offline constant is process-global and forcing it would deadlock a missing model's download."  # b984
